Vita: receipts that say how each particle emitter's particles reached the GPU (twv_vita_particle_
batch_note, platform/vita/runtime/visual_skips.cpp). Dusklight draws most emitters' particles as
one batch of quads and refuses some (a draw function the batch does not cover, a projected
texture, a particle callback, a colour selection); child particles are never batched. Each emitter
draw is counted by outcome with its number of live particles. Counting only: nothing is drawn
differently.

--- a/libs/JSystem/src/JParticle/JPAResource.cpp
+++ b/libs/JSystem/src/JParticle/JPAResource.cpp
@@ -1001,20 +1001,41 @@ static void batch_restore_gx(JPAEmitterWorkData* work, bool changedTev, bool cha
     }
 }
 
+#if TARGET_VITA
+// Vita (patches/dusklight/0056): each emitter draw tells the platform whether its particles went
+// out as one batch and, if not, why (receipts particle_batch_*, platform/vita/runtime/
+// visual_skips.hpp). Counting only; nothing is drawn differently.
+// Outcomes: 0 batched, 1 a draw function the batch does not cover, 2 projected texture, 3 a
+// particle callback, 4 a colour selection the batch does not cover, 5 child particles (drawC
